# Filters

Canonical navigation hierarchy: `root -> dashboard -> tab -> [sections -> widgets]`.

RBAC note: filters shape data inside an already accessible dashboard. They do not grant access and must not be described as an authorization mechanism.

Filters can be defined at dashboard, tab, section, or widget (inline) level. They cascade down: widget inherits section -> tab -> dashboard filters.

## Filter definition

```yaml
filters:
  - id: date_range                     # Required. Unique identifier
    type: date_range                   # Required. See filter types below
    column: install_date               # Required (nullable). Column this filter targets in SQL
    label: Date Range                  # Optional in YAML (inferred from id at runtime)
    placeholder: Select...             # Optional. Override default text shown when no value is set
    #   Defaults: "Select options" (select), "Select date range" (date_range),
    #             "Select range" (relative_date), "Search..." (search)
    icon: Calendar                     # Optional. Lucide icon name
    required: true                     # Optional. Must have a value
    clearable: true                    # Optional. Allow clearing value to empty (default: true)
    #   Applies to: select (single-select), segmented (single-select)
    #   When cleared, SQL renders as 1=1 (no filter). Opt out with clearable: false
    searchable: true                   # Optional. Enable search in select filters
    ui_only: false                     # Optional. If true, filter doesn't affect SQL
    serializable: true                 # Optional. If true, filter is serialized to URL (see URL serialization below)
    pool: geo                          # Optional. Named pool — hidden by default, shown via "+ Add filter"
    source: {}                         # Optional. How to get filter options
    selection: {}                      # Optional. Selection behavior
    default: {}                        # Optional. Default value
    presets: []                        # Optional. Predefined value presets
    true_label: "Yes"                  # Optional. Boolean only: label for true state (default: "Yes")
    false_label: "No"                  # Optional. Boolean only: label for false state (default: "No")
    true_value: 1                      # Optional. Boolean only: SQL literal for true (default: 1)
    false_value: 0                     # Optional. Boolean only: SQL literal for false (default: 0)
    allow_none: false                  # Optional. Segmented only: allow deselecting all (default: false)
    icon_only: false                   # Optional. Segmented only: show only icons, labels as tooltips
```

## Filter types

| Type | UI Component | Value Type |
| ---- | ------------ | ---------- |
| `select` | MultiSelect dropdown | `string[]` or `string` |
| `date_range` | DateRangePicker with presets | `{ start, end, preset? }` |
| `relative_date` | Select with preset options | `{ preset }` |
| `number_range` | Min/max inputs | `{ min?, max? }` |
| `search` | Text input | `string` |
| `boolean` | Two-state toggle (Yes/No) | `boolean` |
| `segmented` | Toggle group | `string \| string[]` |

## Boolean filter

Two-state toggle (Yes/No). Always has a value — `default` is required.

```yaml
- id: is_organic
  type: boolean
  column: is_organic
  label: Organic
  default: false

# Custom labels
- id: is_active
  type: boolean
  column: is_active
  label: Status
  true_label: Active
  false_label: Inactive
  default: true

# Custom SQL values (for non-standard boolean columns)
- id: status
  type: boolean
  column: status
  label: Status
  true_value: "'active'"
  false_value: "'inactive'"
  default: true
```

SQL output: `column = 1` or `column = 0` by default. With `true_value`/`false_value`: `column = <true_value>` or `column = <false_value>`.

## Segmented filter

Toggle group with SQL rendering. Supports static options, SQL-loaded options, multi-select, and icon-only mode. Single-select segmented is clearable by default (click the active segment to deselect). Opt out with `clearable: false`. `allow_none: true` also enables deselection (backward compat).

```yaml
# Single-select (default)
- id: platform
  type: segmented
  column: platform
  default: ios
  source:
    type: static
    options:
      - { value: ios, label: iOS, icon: Apple }
      - { value: android, label: Android, icon: Smartphone }

# Multi-select with deselect
- id: device
  type: segmented
  column: device_type
  allow_none: true
  source:
    type: static
    options:
      - { value: phone, label: Phone }
      - { value: tablet, label: Tablet }
      - { value: desktop, label: Desktop }

# SQL-loaded options
- id: country
  type: segmented
  column: country
  source:
    sql: "SELECT DISTINCT country FROM {{source:main}} ORDER BY country LIMIT 8"

# Icon-only UI toggle
- id: view_mode
  type: segmented
  column: null
  ui_only: true
  default: table
  icon_only: true
  source:
    type: static
    options:
      - { value: table, label: Table view, icon: Table }
      - { value: chart, label: Chart view, icon: BarChart }
```

SQL rendering:
- Single value: `column = 'value'`
- Multi-select: `column IN ('a', 'b')`
- No selection (clearable / allow_none): `1=1`
- No column: `1=1` (ui_only behavior)

## Select single-select mode

When `selection.max_selected: 1`, the select filter switches to single-select mode:

- Auto-applies on click (no Apply button)
- No checkboxes, include/exclude toggle, or select-all
- Shows selected label instead of "1 selected"
- Popover closes on selection
- Clearable by default — click the selected value to deselect, or use the X button. Opt out with `clearable: false`
- When cleared, SQL renders as `1=1` (no filter applied)

```yaml
- id: currency
  type: select
  column: currency
  label: Currency
  source:
    type: static
    options:
      - { value: USD, label: "US Dollar" }
      - { value: EUR, label: Euro }
      - { value: GBP, label: "British Pound" }
  selection:
    max_selected: 1
  default: USD
```

## Filter sources

### Static options

```yaml
source:
  type: static
  options:
    - { value: ios, label: iOS }
    - { value: android, label: Android, icon: Smartphone }
    - { value: web, label: Web, disabled: true }
```

### Query (SQL from ClickHouse)

```yaml
source:
  type: query
  sql: "SELECT DISTINCT media_source FROM marts.marketing_creatives"
  value_field: media_source            # Optional. Column for value
  label_field: media_source            # Optional. Column for label
```

### Projection (from DuckDB projection)

```yaml
source:
  type: projection
  projection: daily_costs_by_source    # Projection key
  value_field: media_source            # Required. Column for value
  label_field: media_source            # Optional. Column for label
  order_by: media_source               # Optional. Sort column
  limit: 100                           # Optional. Max options
```

### Cascade (depends on another filter)

```yaml
source:
  type: cascade
  depends_on: media_source             # Parent filter id
```

### Remote (server-side search)

```yaml
source:
  type: remote
  search_endpoint: /api/search/campaigns
  min_search_length: 2                 # Optional. Min chars before search
```

## Selection behavior

```yaml
selection:
  empty_means: all                     # all | none. What empty selection means
  allow_select_all: true               # Show "Select all" button
  allow_exclude_mode: true             # Allow switching to exclude mode
  min_selected: 1                      # Min items required
  max_selected: 5                      # Max items allowed
```

## Presets (for date_range)

```yaml
presets:
  - { id: today, label: Today, tag: Live }
  - { id: yesterday, label: Yesterday, tag: Live }
  - { id: last_7_days, label: "Last 7 days", tag: Rolling }
  - { id: last_14_days, label: "Last 14 days", tag: Rolling }
  - { id: last_30_days, label: "Last 30 days", tag: Rolling }
  - { id: this_month, label: "This month" }
  - { id: last_month, label: "Last month" }
  - { id: last_6_months, label: "Last 6 months" }
  - { id: last_12_months, label: "Last 12 months" }
default:
  preset: last_14_days
```

## Default values

```yaml
# Preset reference
default:
  preset: last_14_days

# Direct value
default: "ios"

# Array
default: [ios, android]

# Range
default:
  start: "2024-01-01"
  end: "2024-12-31"

# Number range
default:
  min: 0
  max: 100
```

## Filter hierarchy

Dashboard filters -> tab filters -> section filters -> widget inline_filters.

Widgets can control which inherited filters apply:

```yaml
widgets:
  - id: my_widget
    type: rich_table
    filters:
      include: [date_range]            # Only use these from parent scopes
    # OR
    filters:
      exclude: [media_source]          # Use all except these
    inline_filters:                    # Widget-scoped filters
      - id: local_filter
        type: select
        column: status
        source:
          type: static
          options:
            - { value: active, label: Active }
            - { value: paused, label: Paused }
```

## Section-level filter example

```yaml
sections:
  - id: total-by-ad
    title: Total by Ad
    filters:
      - id: media_source
        type: select
        column: media_source
        label: Media Source
        source:
          type: projection
          projection: daily_costs_by_source
          value_field: media_source
          label_field: media_source
        selection:
          empty_means: all
    widgets: [...]
```

## Directory-based dashboards: shared filters

In directory-based dashboards, filters can be defined in `_shared/_filters.yaml`:

```yaml
# _shared/_filters.yaml — array, replaces dashboard-level filters
- id: date_range
  type: date_range
  column: install_date
  default:
    preset: last_14_days
```

Override rule: `_shared/_filters.yaml` **replaces** dashboard-level filters entirely (not merged).

### Tab-level filter override

Composite tabs (directory tabs) can override dashboard-level filters via `<tab>/_shared/_filters.yaml`:

```
dashboards/
  my-dashboard/
    _shared/_filters.yaml          ← dashboard-level (base)
    01-overview/
      _tab.yaml                    ← meta only (id, title)
      _shared/_filters.yaml        ← tab-level override (replaces dashboard filters for this tab)
      01-section.yaml
```

Priority: `<tab>/_shared/_filters.yaml` > section-file `filters:` > dashboard `_shared/_filters.yaml`.

**Deprecated:** defining `filters:` directly in composite tab `_tab.yaml`. Move to `<tab>/_shared/_filters.yaml` instead.

## Smart Table Search (`global_search`)

Smart search is a widget-level feature for `rich_table`. It is **not** a filter type in the traditional filter hierarchy — it works by injecting inline column filters dynamically.

- Configured via `filtering.global_search` in the widget YAML (see `dashboard-rich-table` rule for full docs)
- Uses Orama FTS in-memory index built from DuckDB dimension values
- Resolved tokens are converted to `ColumnFiltersState` entries and applied as inline filters (highlighted in blue)
- Does not participate in the dashboard → section filter cascade

```yaml
# In a rich_table widget:
filtering:
  global_search:
    enabled: true
    show_token_pills: false    # Optional. Show parsed-tokens badge
    token_pills_expanded: true # Optional. Start pills tray expanded (default: true)
```

## Inline column filters (rich_table)

Column-level filters configured via `filtering.show_filter_row: true` use bi-directional cross-filtering: each select filter's dropdown shows only values that exist given **all other** active inline filters, regardless of column order.

- Filters are independent — changing one does not reset others.
- If a selected value disappears from available options (due to other filter changes), it is auto-pruned from the selection.
- Works with all datasource types: base sources, projections, view datasources.
- Text, number, and date inline filters also contribute to cross-filtering for select columns.
- Data presets change the base SQL, so select options reflect the active preset's data subset.

### Smart search interaction

Smart search (`global_search`) results participate in cross-filtering:

1. **Narrow options** — when a search query resolves to column filters (e.g. `en fb` → `language=en, media_source=fb`), select dropdowns for other columns narrow accordingly. Virtual search IDs (`__search_text`, negations, ranges) are ignored.
2. **Lock controls** — columns whose value comes from smart search are disabled (user cannot override the search-derived value). A blue ring indicates the locked state.
3. **Clear restores** — clearing the search input removes all search-derived values and re-enables all controls.

## Root-level shared filters

A root can define shared filters in `_shared/_filters.yaml` (next to `+layout.yaml`). These are inherited by **all dashboards** in that root that do not define their own filters:

```yaml
# dashboards/<root>/_shared/_filters.yaml — inherited by all dashboards
- id: date_range
  type: date_range
  column: install_date
  default:
    preset: last_14_days
```

Override rule: if a dashboard defines **any** filters via `_shared/_filters.yaml`, root-level filters are completely replaced. If a dashboard defines no dashboard-level filters, root-level filters are inherited.

### Full filter hierarchy

Root-level filters → dashboard filters → tab filters → section filters → widget inline_filters.

## URL serialization

Filters can be serialized to URL for shareable dashboard state. Two modes:

- **Live sync** — dashboard-scope filters are auto-synced to the address bar as `f_<id>=value` via `replaceState` (debounced)
- **Share link** — "Copy link to widget/section" generates a full URL (clipboard only) with scoped filters compressed in a `ctx` param + navigation hash

### `serializable` flag

| Scope | Default | Effect |
| ----- | ------- | ------ |
| Dashboard filters | `true` | Auto-synced to URL; opt-out via `serializable: false` |
| Section filters | `false` | Included in share link only if `serializable: true` |
| Widget inline filters | `false` | Included in share link only if `serializable: true` |

```yaml
# Dashboard filter — serialized by default, no change needed
filters:
  - id: date_range
    type: date_range
    column: install_date

  # Opt-out for ui_only filters that have no sharing value
  - id: comparison
    type: segmented
    ui_only: true
    serializable: false

# Section filter — opt-in
sections:
  - id: funnel
    filters:
      - id: funnel_step
        type: select
        column: step
        serializable: true       # included in share link
```

### URL format

| Value type | Format | Example |
| ---------- | ------ | ------- |
| String | raw | `f_status=active` |
| Array (include) | comma-separated | `f_channel=fb,google` |
| Array (exclude) | `!` prefix | `f_channel=!fb,google` |
| Date range (custom) | `start~end` | `f_date_range=2024-01-01~2024-02-01` |
| Date range (preset) | `preset:<id>` | `f_date_range=preset:last_30_days` |
| Boolean | `true`/`false` | `f_active=true` |
| Segmented (single) | raw | `f_platform=ios` |
| Segmented (multi) | comma-separated | `f_device=phone,tablet` |

### Section & widget navigation

Sections and widgets have DOM `id` attributes (`id="s-{sectionId}"`, `id="w-{widgetId}"`) and support hash-based navigation:

```text
/dashboards/<root>/<dashboard>/<tab>#s:section_id       → scroll to section
/dashboards/<root>/<dashboard>/<tab>#w:widget_id        → scroll to widget
```

Collapsed sections auto-expand when navigated to.

### `shareable` flag on sections/widgets

Sections and widgets support `shareable: true` (default for sections with titles, and widgets with titles). This shows a share button that generates a link with the current filter context + navigation anchor.

## Filter pools

Filters can be assigned to named **pools** for progressive disclosure. Filters without a `pool` are always visible; filters with a `pool` are hidden by default and available via a "+ Add filter" button in the filter bar.

```yaml
filters:
  # Always visible — no pool
  - id: date_range
    type: date_range
    column: dt
    default:
      preset: last_14_days

  - id: platform
    type: select
    column: platform
    source:
      type: query
      sql: "SELECT DISTINCT platform AS value, platform AS label FROM {{source:main}}"

  # Hidden by default — pool: language
  - id: native_language
    type: select
    column: native_language
    label: Native language
    pool: language
    source:
      type: query
      sql: "SELECT DISTINCT native_language AS value, native_language AS label FROM {{source:main}}"

  - id: learning_language
    type: select
    column: learning_language
    label: Learning language
    pool: language
    source:
      type: query
      sql: "SELECT DISTINCT learning_language AS value, learning_language AS label FROM {{source:main}}"
```

Pool labels are auto-derived from the pool id: `snake_case / kebab-case → Title Case` (e.g. `campaign_details` → "Campaign Details").

**Restriction:** A filter with `pool` cannot also have `default`. A hidden pool filter with a default value would silently filter data — always remove either `pool` or `default`.

User customization (which pool filters are shown) persists in localStorage via Zustand store.

## SQL template syntax

In base source SQL (ClickHouse), use `${filters.filter_id('column_expression')}`:

```sql
WHERE ${filters.date_range('toDate(install_date)')}
  AND ${filters.media_source('media_source')}
```
